-- A default report disclaimer (owner, 2026-11-24: "set this as the default disclaimer. Remove
-- any proper nouns"). New shops start with it; a shop that offers leak detection and never set
-- one gets it now. Shops with their own text keep it, and a shop can still change or clear it
-- in Settings › Report Terms. Reports already sent keep the text they were sent with.

alter table public.company alter column report_disclaimer set default $text$A leak detection addresses only those components and conditions that are present, visible and accessible at the time of the leak detection. While there may be other parts, components or systems present, only those items specifically noted as being checked were tested for leaks. The inspector performing the leak detection service is not required to move furnishings or stored items. The leak detection report may address issues that are code-based or may refer to a particular code; however, this is NOT a code compliance leak detection report and does NOT verify compliance with manufacturer's installation instructions. This leak detection report is not a property zoning or easement report and will not address such issues. The leak detection does NOT imply insurability or warrantability of the structure or its components. In this report, the inspector performing the leak detection will note which systems and components were tested. The leak detection may not reveal all deficiencies due to hidden or unknown factors. This report is the exclusive property of the company that performed the leak detection and the client whose name appears herewith, and its use by any unauthorized persons is strictly prohibited. The observations and opinions expressed within this report are those of the company that performed the leak detection and supersede any alleged verbal comments. We tested all of the systems, components, and conditions as described above for leaks and cannot be responsible for any work performed in order to cover or hide said leak(s). In accordance with the findings above, the recommendations that we make in this report should be addressed. Customer agrees that in all cases our liability shall be limited to liquidated damages in an amount not greater than the fee you paid us. You waive any claim for consequential, exemplary, special or incidental damages. You acknowledge that the liquidated damages are not a penalty, but that we intend them to (1) reflect the fact that actual damages may be difficult and impractical to ascertain; (2) allocate risk between us; and (3) enable us to perform the leak detection for the agreed upon fee. Customer agrees that any litigation arising out of this report shall be filed only in the court having jurisdiction in the county where we have our principal place of business. If you fail to prove any claim against us, you agree to pay all our legal costs, expenses and fees incurred in defending that claim. You agree that any legal action against us, allegedly arising out of this report, must be brought only in the district court having jurisdiction in the county where we have our principal place of business. Before bringing any such action, you must provide us with 30 days' written notice of the nature of the claim. In any action against us you waive trial by jury. If a court declares any provision of this report invalid, the remaining provisions remain in effect. This report represents leak detection findings; there are no terms or promises set forth herein. No statement or promise by us shall be binding unless reduced to writing and signed by one of our authorized officers. You will have no cause of action against us after one year from the date of the leak detection. If a court finds any term of this report ambiguous or that it otherwise requires judicial interpretation, the court shall not construe that term against us by reason of the rule that any ambiguity in a document is construed against the party drafting it.$text$;

-- Pool-only shops don't see Report Terms in Settings, so they aren't given leak detection terms.
update public.company set report_disclaimer = default
where nullif(trim(report_disclaimer), '') is null
  and coalesce(settings ->> 'services', 'both') <> 'pool';
